    "english":  "Like eager men who worship their beloved deity with unyielding devotion\nand at last behold the god face to face,\nall our long weariness and trembling sorrow have melted away,\nfor we have reached your gentle, rounded, bamboo-like arms!\nTherefore, O maiden of sparkling white teeth,\nrub the glowing, tender leaves of the red punkam tree\nupon your breast bright with beauty-spots to soothe their longing.\nLinger at ease beneath every welcoming shade;\npause to make small houses in every bank of white sand.\nWalk slowly, without distress, along the forest pathΓÇö\nfor cool groves resound with joyful cuckoos pecking at mango buds,\nand hospitable villages lie close along our way.",
